# Every file in this repo is served verbatim over HTTP from GitHub Pages and
# verified by the app against a SHA-256 recorded in index.json.
#
# That makes line endings load-bearing. With core.autocrlf=true and no rules
# here, a checkout rewrites LF to CRLF in the working tree; build_manifest.py
# then hashes the CRLF copy while GitHub Pages serves the LF copy stored in git.
# Every checksum comes out wrong by exactly one byte per line, and the app
# rejects the download as corrupt — which is what happened on 2026-08-14, when
# 11 of 14 files failed verification on device.
#
# Forcing LF in the working tree keeps what we hash byte-identical to what we
# serve. Do not remove this without changing how checksums are computed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the files the app actually verifies.
*.json text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
